  "body": "`xtask` already discovers directory suites (`tests/<suite>/main.rs`, #927), but three places still assume flat test files or run the whole binary:\n\n- `xtask/src/assets.rs:48` reads only `crates/<d>/tests/{b}.rs`. Folding any post or machine test into a directory suite breaks `#923` asset selection.\n- `xtask/src/catalog.rs:146` checks `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs` instead of `suites::entry(root, \"app\", \"example_catalog\")`.\n- `xtask/src/plan.rs:181` (`may_run_ignored`) returns `true` whenever `mod x;` appears in `main.rs`, so every directory suite gets a heavy step even without `#[ignore]` tests.\n- `xtask/src/quick.rs:186-195` (`map_modules`) merges Gate maps across all submodules of a directory suite and runs the whole binary (`p.whole`). Editing helper code inside one submodule also runs the whole binary (`quick.rs:103-133`).\n\nUpdate `assets.rs`, `catalog.rs`, and `plan::may_run_ignored` to walk `suites::sources` / `suites::entry`. Update `quick.rs` to match Gate maps per source file (`suites::Source`) and pass libtest module filters (`--test <suite> <submod>::`) when only specific submodules match or when one submodule changes outside `#[test]` fns. Fall back to the whole binary only when `main.rs` or a shared module changes.\n\nEvidence and measurements: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-7065686766\n\nDone means: `xtask` unit tests verify that a directory suite triggers `#923` asset selection, `#2393` catalog selection, accurate `may_run_ignored` detection, and `<submod>::` selection in `quick`.\n\nPart of #919\n",
